# ── Secrets — real credential values NEVER go in git ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Placeholders like <PFX_PW> live in tracked files; the real values live ONLY in SECRETS.local.md,
# which travels by your own secure channel (an encrypted vault / a USB / a password manager) —
# never the repo. This denylist is defense-in-depth: the hooks auto-commit + auto-push, so a stray
# credential file in a tracked dir would otherwise land on your remote.
SECRETS.local.md
**/SECRETS.local.md
SECRETS.md
*.secret
*.secrets
nas-credential.txt
**/nas-credential.txt
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.keystore
*.ppk
credentials.json
**/credentials.json
id_rsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
*_rsa
*_ed25519

# Your per-machine remote config (set from config.example.ps1) — machine-specific, never shared.
/setup/config.ps1

# Code repositories you add under Projects/ are independently version-controlled (their own remotes).
/Projects/*/

# Raw session transcripts: large, and they contain every tool result verbatim (credential-bearing).
# Only the redacted, conversation-only rendered/ tier is tracked.
/transcripts/raw/
/transcripts/.render-state.json
/transcripts/mirror-target.txt
# Per-machine selective-drift target + its verdict cache (see transcripts/README.md).
/transcripts/drift-target.txt
/transcripts/.drift-state.json

# Python + OS cruft
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Cloud-sync conflict copies, so a bad resync never gets committed as canon
*conflict*
*Conflict*
* (1)*
